FMCSA has several options for enforcing these regulations. In order to register with FMCSA, brokers must agree to comply with all applicable regulations (
49 U.S.C. 13904(a)(2)
), and FMCSA has the authority to suspend or revoke a broker's operating authority for willful failure to comply with a condition of registration (
49 U.S.C. 13905(d)(2)(A)(iii)
). FMCSA may also decline to renew a broker's registration if the broker has demonstrated it is not willing or able to comply with the regulations.
